   * The endpoint requires a valid section identifier in the path parameter, which scopes the article retrieval to that specific section. Articles are filtered by the discussion_board_section_id foreign key relationship, ensuring only articles belonging to the specified section are returned. This relationship enforces that each article must belong to exactly one section for organizational purposes.
   *
   * Search capabilities include partial title matching using GIN trigram indexing on the title field, body content filtering using GIN trigram indexing on the body field, and date range queries based on the created_at timestamp. Results are returned in paginated format with configurable page size and sorting options (newest first or oldest first via created_at ordering). The response includes article summaries with essential metadata such as title, author information from the discussion_board_members relationship, creation timestamp, and dynamically computed comment count.
   *
   * Soft-deleted articles (those with deleted_at timestamp set) are automatically excluded from results, maintaining data integrity while preserving article history for administrative purposes. The discussion_board_articles table supports soft deletion to preserve content history while removing articles from public views. Administrators can permanently remove articles through separate administrative operations.
   *
   * The section validation ensures the target section exists and is not soft-deleted before returning articles. If the section does not exist or is soft-deleted, an empty list is returned to maintain consistent behavior.
   *
   * @param connection
